/-!
# Compatible fields and the Cartan contradiction

This interface exposes the constructed compatible fields, literal marked
sections, invariant complements, both full Cartan scalar families, and
terminal weights. The source contradiction is available both through
the direct displacement proof of bilinearity and through the two scalar
families. Each route retains only the preceding common-core geometry
and independent action markings for the source assembly owner.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 11.3.8--9 and Proposition 11.3.2, printed
pp.774--775.
-/
